! C2H7O3Cl | Equilibrium Geometry
! wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water)
! def2-TZVPP basis via BASNAM, sourced from Basis Set Exchange (Turbomole 7.3 data)
! No constraints
!
! Provenance / changes vs. caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPP.inp and ...TZVPPa.inp:
! - TZVPP.inp: requested $HESS HESS=READ with no Hessian data actually supplied;
!   GAMESS silently fell back to HESS=GUESS. Optimization proceeded but the
!   BFGS-updated Hessian developed an increasingly negative curvature eigenvalue
!   (-15 -> -18 -> -30 -> -57 across successive steps) and the structure collapsed
!   (multiple H...H / X...H distances under 1.0 Angstrom in the final geometry).
! - TZVPPa.inp: same molecule, no $HESS/$GUESS override (defaulted to HUCKEL).
!   Did not collapse, but 84 individual SCF single-points computed during the
!   NSERCH=5 numerical Hessian block (tiny finite-difference displacements)
!   scattered across ~0.18 Hartree (~113 kcal/mol) -- clear evidence of the SCF
!   landing on different, inconsistent electronic solutions step to step.
!   Run aborted at NSERCH=5 with GRADIENT OUT OF RANGE.
! - Both runs used $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM despite GAMESS explicitly reporting
!   analytic gradients were available for this SCFTYP/DFTTYP/PCM combination.
!   Semi-numerical gradients are noisier; that noise feeds directly into the
!   BFGS Hessian update, plausibly explaining both the runaway negative
!   curvature (TZVPP) and the erratic per-step SCF/gradient behaviour (TZVPPa).
!
! This version (b):
! - Uses METHOD=ANALYTIC (removes the confirmed noise source)
! - No $HESS or $GUESS override -- clean HUCKEL default, no stale-file risk
! - SOSCF=.T. restored (GAMESS's own more robust default; testing showed
!   SOSCF was NOT the cause of the TZVPP collapse, so no reason to avoid it)
! - NOTE: first submission attempt of this file mistakenly set DIIS=.T.
!   together with SOSCF=.T. GAMESS treats these as mutually exclusive
!   convergers and aborted immediately (error 911) before any SCF cycle.
!   Fixed by removing DIIS=.T. and keeping SOSCF=.T. alone.
! - NOTE (correction): $FORCE METHOD actually governs how the HESSIAN is
!   computed (needed for HSSEND=.T. and periodic IHREP recomputation),
!   NOT the routine per-step optimization gradient -- that was already
!   analytic by default in every prior run (NUMGRD=F). Requesting
!   METHOD=ANALYTIC triggers GAMESS's analytic DFT Hessian, which has
!   5 requirements; RHF and non-meta-GGA were already satisfied, so
!   NOSYM=1, DIRSCF=.TRUE., and $CPHF CPHF=AO were added to satisfy the
!   rest, avoiding a fallback to the numerical-Hessian noise we are
!   trying to eliminate in the first place.
! - Cartesian coordinates (DLC=.F. AUTO=.F.) rather than delocalized internal
!   coordinates, since this is a weakly-bound 3-molecule H-bonded cluster and
!   automatic bond perception across long/weak intermolecular contacts is a
!   plausible additional source of a poorly conditioned optimization -- worth
!   isolating as a variable given TZVPP (which collapsed) used DLC=.T. AUTO=.T.
!   and TZVPPa (which did not collapse) used Cartesian.
! - Removed the stray empty $DATA block that appeared before the basis set
!   definitions in TZVPPa.inp (harmless but untidy).

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         COORD=UNIQUE MAXIT=200 NOSYM=1
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS BASNAM(1)=clbas,cbas,cbas,obas,hbas,hbas,
          obas,obas,hbas,hbas,hbas,hbas,hbas $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $CPHF CPHF=AO $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.0001 NSTEP=300 IHREP=5 HSSEND=.T. DXMAX=0.05 NPRT=1 $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.F. AUTO=.F. $END
 $FORCE METHOD=ANALYTIC PROJCT=.T. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=100 MEMDDI=200 $END

 $DATA
Chloroacetaldehyde hydrate and water
C1
Cl   17.0   3.31777   0.19618   0.40668
C     6.0   2.24118   0.90662  -0.95961
C     6.0   3.04189   1.88482  -1.77661
O     8.0   2.47874   2.79975  -2.40567
H     1.0   1.37854   1.36717  -0.48364
H     1.0   1.95549   0.05691  -1.58084
O     8.0   3.58112   0.05498  -3.89961
O     8.0   3.79699   2.62132  -4.86879
H     1.0   3.58756   3.03704  -5.71005
H     1.0   3.65634   0.88740  -4.40943
H     1.0   2.96923  -0.51508  -4.37329
H     1.0   4.12539   1.74751  -1.81197
H     1.0   3.29383   3.07126  -4.16999
 $END


